    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q2a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$-2,\\ \\frac14,\\ -1,\\ \\frac{-5}{-3},\\ -\\frac75,\\ \\frac12,\\ 1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2<-\\frac75<-1<\\frac14<\\frac12<1<\\frac{-5}{-3}$",
          "worked": "The double-negative fraction is positive: $\\frac{-5}{-3}=\\frac53$. Compare the negative numbers using fifths: $-2=-\\frac{10}{5}<-\\frac75<-\\frac55=-1$. For the positive numbers, $\\frac14<\\frac24<1<\\frac53$. Therefore,\n$$-2<-\\frac75<-1<\\frac14<\\frac12<1<\\frac{-5}{-3}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q2b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$-\\frac74,\\ \\frac{-11}{-3},\\ -\\frac{11}{5},\\ \\frac{14}{5},\\ \\frac72$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{11}{5}<-\\frac74<\\frac{14}{5}<\\frac72<\\frac{-11}{-3}$",
          "worked": "The double-negative fraction is positive: $\\frac{-11}{-3}=\\frac{11}{3}$. Compare the negative fractions: $-\\frac{11}{5}=-\\frac{44}{20}<-\\frac{35}{20}=-\\frac74$. Compare the positive fractions using thirtieths: $\\frac{14}{5}=\\frac{84}{30}<\\frac{105}{30}=\\frac72<\\frac{110}{30}=\\frac{11}{3}$. Therefore,\n$$-\\frac{11}{5}<-\\frac74<\\frac{14}{5}<\\frac72<\\frac{-11}{-3}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q2c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$-\\frac23,\\ -\\frac45,\\ -\\frac{11}{12},\\ \\frac{12}{13}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{11}{12}<-\\frac45<-\\frac23<\\frac{12}{13}$",
          "worked": "Use a common denominator for the negative fractions:\n$$-\\frac{11}{12}=-\\frac{55}{60}<-\\frac{48}{60}=-\\frac45<-\\frac{40}{60}=-\\frac23.$$\nThe positive fraction is greater than every negative fraction. Therefore,\n$$-\\frac{11}{12}<-\\frac45<-\\frac23<\\frac{12}{13}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q2d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$-1\\frac{11}{13},\\ -\\frac{15}{13},\\ -2,\\ -1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-2<-1\\frac{11}{13}<-\\frac{15}{13}<-1$",
          "worked": "Write every number in thirteenths: $-2=-\\frac{26}{13}$, $-1\\frac{11}{13}=-\\frac{24}{13}$ and $-1=-\\frac{13}{13}$. Since $-26<-24<-15<-13$,\n$$-2<-1\\frac{11}{13}<-\\frac{15}{13}<-1.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
